+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value |
+| ------ | ----- |
+| Issue  | #37   |
+| Status | Draft |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the tool's declared `inputSchema` before the executor runs. A rejection is returned as a `ToolResponse`; only an unknown tool name throws.
+
+- Input missing a required property is rejected with a result naming the property, and the executor is not invoked ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property without running the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L24)).
+- A wrong-typed field is rejected with a result naming its path and expected type, and neither the result nor any log line contains an input value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming its path and expected type, never its value or in logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L36)).
+- Valid input with an unlisted extra property reaches the executor unchanged, exactly once ([validated by: passes valid input with an unlisted extra property to the executor unchanged, once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L56)).
+- Registering a tool whose schema cannot be compiled throws at registration, naming the tool ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
+- A function-valued definition is validated against the schema it resolves to at that call, not a cached earlier one ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L76)).
